## Product Context

### Scope and boundary

**In scope** — the product and its interfaces: reader, controller, request-to-exit,
management server, and the cloud/RDPS portal (RDPS is part of the product per §6.2).

**Out of scope** — external systems the product interfaces with but does not include;
only the interface is assessed, not their internals:

- **[OOS-1]** Fire alarm panel — trusted to assert release [ENV-6]; only the override input is in scope.
- **[OOS-2]** Building IP network — shared infrastructure [ENV-3]; treated as an untrusted conduit.
- **[OOS-3]** Door, frame, and mechanical lock body — _scope call: in if part of the product (in-handle), out if procured separately_; the electric-release interface [FN-2] is in scope regardless.

**Applies to** — this model covers the product across a range of hardware revisions
and software versions, not a single build. It holds while each component stays within
its assessed range; a component that moves outside it is re-assessed. The exact
revision a deployed unit runs is pinned per build in the release manifest (component →
repo → revision), not here.

